# Generated from CLion Inspection settings.
#
# One entry is hand-added below CLion's list: -performance-faster-string-find.
# `performance-*` pulls it in, but clang-tidy 23 reports it as deprecated, and
# that arrives as a [clang-tidy-config] diagnostic which -warnings-as-errors=*
# promotes to a hard error on every single file — the build could never pass
# with it enabled. Its suggested replacement,
# performance-prefer-single-char-overloads, is already disabled in this
# profile, so turning the deprecated one off matches the intent.
---
Checks: '-*,
mpi-*,
bugprone-suspicious-realloc-usage,
bugprone-terminating-continue,
bugprone-misplaced-operator-in-strlen-in-alloc,
